on-arrival: bruning_skibidi_time = time + 3 if not reparations_resolved
set-bg: img/map_2.jpg

= Public Works Mobilization Act

With Askew focused on securing a foreign policy victory, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord":<span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord":<span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]'s Labor Minister Adam Sedgewick and the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]'s Vice Chancellor and Finance Minister Albrecht Dietrich have been developing a job creation program. The <span style="color: #6D5298;">Christian Socials</span> and several <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> figures, such as Günther Gereke, have also backed this approach. However, given the state of the national budget, such a program was not feasible without either severe welfare cuts or a breakthrough on War Loans—delaying action until now due to fears of public backlash.

Dietrich has since secured Assembly approval to raise 1.4 billion Gold through a bond issue to fund the initiative. [? if not reparations_resolved: Yet the Commonwealth Bank remains reluctant to provide support, at least not until the War Loans issue is resolved at Vera in the coming months. As a result, Dietrich’s proposal has been sharply scaled back, with only 160 million Gold allocated and further austerity measures introduced in the upcoming act. The act’s centerpiece is the establishment of a new "Voluntary Labor Service" brigade, tasked with draining swamps and digging artificial lakes—at subminimum wages. ?][? if reparations_resolved: With War Loans now resolved at Vera, the Commonwealth Bank feels more comfortable authorizing spending. The act's centerpiece is the creation of a new "Voluntary Labor Service" brigade, tasked with draining swamps and digging artificial lakes—at subminimum wages. ?]

[? if not reparations_resolved: Should Vera bring success, full funding for Dietrich’s program may still follow. Askew's coalition just has to survive until then. ?]

- @wait

@wait
title: We will vote for the act, and so will the propertied parties. [? if gold_exist and not lvp_formed: (barring the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>)?][? if lvp_formed: (barring the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s industrialists)?]
on-arrival: labor_dissent -= 5; wtb_points += 200; dufour_angry_bruning -= 50; gold_left += 5; ddp_left += 3; lvp_left += 3; ddp_cohesion += 3; unionist_relation += 5 if wtb_adopted; ddp_relation += 5 if wtb_adopted; lvp_relation += 5 if wtb_adopted; disfavored -= 3; inflation += 2; budget -= 1; economic_growth += 2; commons_royalist -= 2; commons_ddp += 1; commons_unionist += 1; commons_traditionalist += 1; commons_lvp += 1; disfavored_royalist -= 3; disfavored_unionist += 2; disfavored_ddp += 2; disfavored_traditionalist += 2; disfavored_lvp += 2
go-to: public_works_pt2 if reparations_resolved

With strong support from the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord":<span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord":<span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], General Kurt von Staal, and his allies in the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, the bill passes. However, it has provoked the anger of industrialists within the center-right coalition[? if not reparations_resolved:—though the scaled-down scope of the plan has, for now, kept their outrage contained?].

[? if reparations_resolved: Despite Askew’s longstanding belief that public works should follow the bottoming out of the depression, it appears he now sees that moment as having arrived—with the global recovery and the abolition of Commonwealth War Loans. Still, inflationary fears among the public have constrained any major expansion of the money supply, and the industrialists within the coalition have fought tooth and nail to gut the bill’s more expensive provisions. Fortunately, their votes are not required to pass it. ?]

@public_works_pt2
on-arrival: labor_dissent -= 5; dufour_angry_bruning -= 25; lautenbach_adopted = 1; lautenbach_plan_time = time + 12; public_works_name = "Dietrich"; gold_left += 3; ddp_left += 2; lvp_left += 2; ddp_cohesion += 2; inflation += 2; budget -= 1; economic_growth += 2; commons_royalist -= 1; commons_ddp += 1; commons_unionist += 1; commons_traditionalist += 1; commons_lvp += 1; disfavored_royalist -= 3; disfavored_unionist += 2; disfavored_ddp += 2; disfavored_traditionalist += 2; disfavored_lvp += 2